    <h2 id="what-it-means" class="text-2xl font-bold text-v6-dark mt-12 mb-4 scroll-mt-24">What this means for revenue teams</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] text-v6-text leading-relaxed">
      If you run renewals in HubSpot, this corpus says three things clearly. First, the renewal process is
      where you will get stuck most often, and the trigger is usually mechanical: a workflow that will not
      re-create next year's deal, or a clone that drops the line items. Second, the deepest damage is at
      the seam between HubSpot and your accounting system, where revenue and forecast numbers quietly stop
      being trustworthy. Third, the two problems are the same problem wearing two hats: if the renewal deal
      never forms correctly, or the revenue never reconciles to the ledger, your net revenue retention and
      renewal forecast are running on numbers you already suspect are wrong.
      <strong>Cloning a deal is the easy 10%.</strong> The renewal pipeline, at-risk visibility, escalation
      math, and clean sync to finance are the 90% where the money leaks.
    </p>

